##############################################################################
# Docker build-context filter for the VWRAY control-plane image.
#
# Every entry is either large, secret-bearing or platform-specific. This is not
# only a build-speed concern: anything left in the context can be baked into an
# image layer by `COPY . .`, and image layers are readable by anyone who can pull
# the image. A `.env` or a private key that reaches the context is a leak waiting
# for a careless COPY.
##############################################################################

# ------------------------------------------------- dependencies / build output -
# Installed and produced inside the image (`npm ci`, `prisma generate`,
# `next build`). Copying the host's copies would poison the build with the
# developer's platform-specific binaries.
node_modules
.next
out
build
dist
.swc
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ VCS / IDE --
# `.git` alone is usually the largest object in a repository and is never needed.
.git
.github
.gitignore
.claude
.agents
agent
skills-lock.json
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
*.swp

# ------------------------------------------------------------ secrets & keys --
# The runtime image receives every credential from the orchestrator at run time.
# The only DATABASE_URL in the build is the intentionally dead placeholder passed
# as a build ARG (see the Dockerfile).
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.crt
*.jks
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
known_hosts
.npmrc

# -------------------------------------------------- databases / dumps / backups -
# NOTE: `*.sql` is deliberately NOT ignored - prisma/migrations/**/migration.sql
# is source that the runtime image needs in order to run `migrate deploy`.
backups
*.dump
*.sql.gz
*.tar.gz
coverage
.nyc_output
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# ------------------------------------------------------- ops-only descriptors --
# These change on ops branches and have no effect on the image content. Ignoring
# them keeps the `COPY . .` layer cacheable across infrastructure-only commits.
Dockerfile
Dockerfile.*
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.*.yml
railway.json
render.yaml
Procfile
README.md
docs
LICENSE
CODEOWNERS
